WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:03.600
It's a bird, it's a plane, it's… gone.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.340
Just seven weeks ago, Henry Cavill posted&nbsp;
the news on his Instagram that fans had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:13.140
been waiting for ever since "Zack Snyder's&nbsp;
Justice League." His long-awaited return as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.140 --> 00:00:17.940
Superman sent fans into a frenzy as they&nbsp;
looked forward to his continuation of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.320
character. The celebration was short-lived,&nbsp;
however, with the news breaking on Wednesday&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.720
that Henry Cavill was now out as Superman, and&nbsp;
his role in the DC Universe had come to an end.

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.792
"You did this."

00:00:29.792 --> 00:00:32.635
"I had to."

00:00:32.635 --> 00:00:33.420
"You won't let me live."

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:39.600
James Gunn and his co-CEO of DC Studios, Peter&nbsp;
Safran, have spent the last few weeks holed up and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:44.640
hidden away while they developed what comes next&nbsp;
for DC. And fans have questions regarding who,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:49.740
if anyone, from the Snyderverse will be making&nbsp;
the jump to the new universe about to take shape.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:54.600
Given his most recent announcement, you would be&nbsp;
forgiven if you thought Cavill was a lock to stay&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:59.820
in the role. Unfortunately, Gunn and Safran have&nbsp;
different plans, with the director announcing on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:04.440
Twitter that they're going the younger route&nbsp;
for the Kryptonian, meaning Cavill is out.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.480
The actor also announced his departure from the&nbsp;
role in his own Instagram post, expressing his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:14.820
sadness but also reminding fans that Superman&nbsp;
still lives. Unsurprisingly, the Internet went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:19.320
ablaze, with fans expressing their displeasure&nbsp;
with the decision to remove the British actor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:25.080
when they just got him back. If you're feeling&nbsp;
betrayed, angry, upset, depressed, or simply&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:30.240
dumbfounded, you aren't alone. Social media&nbsp;
has a whole host of people ready to join you.

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:34.560
"Superman is dead. We all wish he wasn't."

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:37.620
The Snyderverse isn't known for&nbsp;
a deep roster of great films,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:43.020
but there are some bright spots within them, and&nbsp;
Henry Cavill was one of them. Although his darker&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.920
portrayal of the character was divisive,&nbsp;
he was largely beloved by the fan base.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:52.140
His dismissal from Superman brought on many&nbsp;
negative takes, including one poster who wrote:

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:56.460
"I could not be more devastated.&nbsp;
In 1 move you have single-handedly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:00.780
destroyed every ounce of interest&nbsp;
and enthusiasm I had for DC movies."

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.900
Another person agreed with the sentiment, saying,

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:05.640
"This legit makes no sense."

00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.260
Someone else eloquently let James Gunn know what&nbsp;
it felt like when they read the news, writing,

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:14.280
"Easily the swiftest most precise&nbsp;
kick to the balls I think anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:17.340
has done with all of Superman's&nbsp;
power in all of DC history."

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:22.500
Of course, Twitter isn't the only outlet where&nbsp;
fans reacted to the news — many also took to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:26.940
Reddit to talk about the revelation that their&nbsp;
favorite Superman actor isn't returning. One&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:30.840
Redditor took a different path and thought&nbsp;
about how Cavill himself must be feeling:

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:34.140
"Wow, that just sucks. I hope he can catch a break&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:36.960
soon. Someone send him some&nbsp;
Warhammer figures to paint."

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.900
Finally, there was one user&nbsp;
who wasn't quite as negative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:42.360
expressing a little interest in what's next:

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:46.920
"Interested to see where James Gunn&nbsp;
takes the DCU but definitely would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.920 --> 00:02:50.820
[have] loved to have seen more of Henry as&nbsp;
Superman. Sucks we don't get to see him as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:55.080
Geralt anymore either. Hopefully he lands&nbsp;
another iconic role in the near future."

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.680
This brings up a good point. With all&nbsp;
the news about Gunn's new direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.980
there are many, many questions&nbsp;
about where he's headed.

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.540
"Consider this mercy."

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:08.400
It shouldn't be surprising that James Gunn and&nbsp;
Peter Safran are cleaning house at DC. While&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:12.840
Disney and Marvel have been doing what Warner&nbsp;
Bros. and DC have been trying to do for a decade,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:17.760
DC is failing where Marvel is succeeding.&nbsp;
Even without their most well-known characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:23.340
Spider-Man, the X-Men, and the Fantastic Four,&nbsp;
Marvel was able to build a universe that changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:28.560
cinema. All the while, DC has taken three of the&nbsp;
most globally well-known characters of all time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.260
Superman, Batman, and Wonder Woman, and mostly&nbsp;
stumbled in its recent handling of them.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:38.580
With the announcement that new leadership&nbsp;
is in store for the DC movies, ushering in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:43.380
new universe with fresh takes and rebooted&nbsp;
storylines seems to be a solid choice. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:47.280
problem is the backlash from a fan base that&nbsp;
wants to see all the aspects they love about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:51.660
the Snyderverse. Of course, this also raises&nbsp;
more questions about the characters we have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:55.920
yet to hear about. What will happen with&nbsp;
Jason Momoa after the release of "Aquaman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.920 --> 00:04:01.200
2"? What about Zachary Levi? Dwayne Johnson?&nbsp;
Is there any point in the Flash movie now?

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.880
Some of them expressed their love and support&nbsp;
for Henry Cavill, with Momoa commenting on his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.380
Instagram post, 
 
"love u brother"

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:08.940
along with heart emojis.

00:04:08.940 --> 00:04:10.140
Levi commented,

00:04:10.140 --> 00:04:12.360
"Hope to catch you in another universe, sir."

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.400
There's no question that the tide is shifting,&nbsp;
and it looks like Gunn and Safran are ditching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:22.440
anything that contains the baggage of the past as&nbsp;
they move forward. Fans have a lot to get over,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.860
and Gunn has to bring something&nbsp;
monumental to help that along.

